sonarqube
# packages/ is not listed, on purpose. Under Linux a restore fills <repository>/packages
# (RestorePackagesPath, Directory.Build.props), and deploy/Dockerfile.host copies the whole
# context: its publish restores from that folder instead of downloading the closure again.
# A fresh checkout (CI) has none, and no image keeps it in its final stage.
#
# Docker anchors a pattern at the root of the context: *.md drops the Markdown of the
# repository root and nothing deeper. The rest stays, on purpose: Dockerfile.runners ships
# the README of every example (`orkeon-example show` prints it) and the documents the
# scripting demos read (examples/scripting/data/), and every build reads the
# AnalyzerReleases.*.md of the VFS analyzer under src/.
*.md
!README.md
# Every image copies these two into /usr/share/doc/orkeon/: the notices go with the bits.
!LICENSE.md
!THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
